  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "GREv1Layer::computeCalculateFields",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/GreLayer.cpp",
    "description": "`GREv1Layer::computeCalculateFields()` unconditionally writes `payloadLength` into the GREv1 header (`getGreHeader()->payloadLength = ...`) without verifying that the layer buffer is large enough to contain a full `gre1_header`. For malformed/truncated GREv1 packets parsed from fuzzed input, `m_DataLen` can be smaller than the required header size, so this 2-byte store lands past the allocated packet buffer (heap-buffer-overflow).",
    "conditions": "In `FuzzTarget`, attacker-controlled bytes are dumped to a pcap file, read into `RawPacket`, parsed into `Packet`, then `parsedPacket.computeCalculateFields()` is called on all parsed layers. If input causes a GREv1 layer to be recognized on a too-short backing buffer (e.g., truncated GREv1 header near packet end), `computeCalculateFields()` reaches the unchecked header write at line ~539 and overflows by 2 bytes at the end of the heap allocation."
  },
